<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soba was the capital of the medieval Nubian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alodia">Alodia</a>, on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Blue Nile</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a>. Medieval writers described it as a large city with fine buildings and churches, and excavations have revealed churches, palaces and imported goods. It declined in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and was abandoned after the Funj and Abdallab took it around 1504.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soba.jpg" alt="Soba" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FotoosVanRobin · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dried_soba_noodles_by_FotoosVanRobin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
